# Codebase Architecture Rules

## File Structure
```
src/
  types/
    {domain}/
      {domain}.types.ts       # interfaces & types
      {domain}.enums.ts       # enums & const objects
      {domain}.form.ts        # UI/form specific types
      {domain}.constants.ts   # static constants
      index.ts                # barrel export for the module
    shared.enums.ts           # enums used across 2+ modules
    shared.types.ts           # types used across 2+ modules
    index.ts                  # global barrel export
  hooks/
    use-{domain}.ts
  components/
    {domain}/
      {ComponentName}.tsx
```

## File Length
- Max 250 lines per file (.tsx)
- Max 150 lines per ts.hook (.ts)
- Max 100 lines per ts.type (.ts,)
- Max 200 lines per other ts (.ts)
- If a file exceeds the max number lines, split by concern

## Naming Conventions

### Interfaces
- PascalCase
- Suffix with intent:
- Suffix with intent:
  - `*Payload`   — data sent TO the API (POST/PUT body)
  - `*Response`  — data received FROM the API
  - `*State`     — local component/form state
  - `*Props`     — React component props
  - `*Config`    — configuration objects
  - `*Options`   — dropdown/select option shapes
- **Module Prefix Convention**: All domain-specific interfaces and enums MUST be prefixed with the domain/module name (e.g., `ProjectResponse`, `ProjectMemberRole`). This prevents naming collisions across modules.
- Extend instead of redeclaring:
```typescript
// ✅
interface CreateProjectPayload extends BaseProjectPayload {
  owner_company_id: string;
}
// ❌
interface CreateProjectPayload {
  owner_company_id: string;
  title: string; // repeated from BaseProjectPayload
}
```

### Enums / Const Objects
### Enums / Const Objects
- Use `as const` objects (not TypeScript enums) so values can be iterated
- PascalCase name, UPPER_SNAKE values only when they are acronyms, otherwise lowercase
- **Module Prefix Convention**: Enums specific to a domain MUST be prefixed with the domain name (e.g., `ProjectStatus`, `ProjectReviewerType`).
- **Use Enums for Comparison**: ALWAYS use the enum properties for comparisons (e.g., `status === ProjectStatus.active`) instead of hardcoding inline string values (`status === "active"`).
```typescript
// ✅ — reusable as type AND iterable as value
export const DurationUnit = {
  days: "days",
  weeks: "weeks",
  months: "months",
  years: "years",
} as const;
export type DurationUnit = (typeof DurationUnit)[keyof typeof DurationUnit];

// ❌ — TypeScript enum, not iterable
enum DurationUnit { days = "days" }
```

### Constants
- SCREAMING_SNAKE_CASE for primitive constants
- PascalCase const objects
```typescript
export const MAX_FILE_SIZE = 5_000_000;
export const QUERY_KEYS = { projects: ["projects"] } as const;
```

### Hooks
- `use-{domain}.ts` filename
- `use{Domain}` function name

## No inline types in .tsx files
## No inline types in .tsx files
- All interfaces, types, enums must live in `types/{domain}/`
- **Shared Types**: If a type or enum is used by 2 or more modules, it must be moved to `types/shared.enums.ts` or `types/shared.types.ts`.
- **Barrel Exports**: Each `{domain}` folder must have an `index.ts` barrel file exporting its contents. The root `types/index.ts` re-exports all domains.
- Exception: anonymous inline prop types for small local subcomponents only

## Imports order (enforced by eslint-plugin-import)
1. React
2. Third-party
3. Absolute `@/`
4. Relative `./`
